// A chain marker is a seam between two segments of one function, not a
// statement: it emits nothing. Without this arm it would fall through to es4,
// which treats anything that is not an `if` as a `while`.
// A chain marker is a seam between two segments of one function, and a `blank`
// is an action slot that does nothing: neither emits anything. Without these
// arms both would fall through to es4, which treats anything that is not an
// `if` as a `while`.
es3b(int id, string ind) {
  if((import nkind)[id] == "iassign") {
    emit_iassign(id, ind);
  } else if((import nkind)[id] != "chain" && (import nkind)[id] != "blank") {
    es_flow(id, ind);
  }
} return void;
